## Fix Round 1 — Close inherited instance storage

Commit: `205ad2d fix: close strategy policy instances`

### Changed code

- Added `__slots__ = ()` to `_CanonicalContract`, preventing frozen slotted contract subclasses from inheriting a mutable instance `__dict__`.
- Added `test_contract_instances_have_no_mutable_instance_dictionary`, which instantiates every snapshot, decision, and nested policy contract and asserts none exposes `__dict__`.

### Test evidence

RED command:

```text
python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_strategy_policy.py -k "mutable_instance_dictionary"
```

RED result: `1 failed, 26 deselected`. The new regression failed at `assert all(not hasattr(contract, "__dict__") for contract in contracts)`, proving the inherited mutable dictionary existed.

GREEN commands:

```text
python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_strategy_policy.py -k "mutable_instance_dictionary"
python -B -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q tests/test_strategy_policy.py
```

GREEN results: the narrow regression reported `1 passed, 26 deselected`; the complete focused policy file reported `27 passed`. Both invocations emitted only the pre-existing pytest `cache_dir` configuration warning.

### Self-review

- Reviewed the two-file diff and ran `git diff --check`; no whitespace errors were present.
- Confirmed the fix is limited to base-class instance layout, so all descendants now lack an inherited `__dict__` without changing serializers, validators, or policy behavior.
- Commit hooks passed ruff, trailing-whitespace, EOF, YAML, and merge-conflict checks.
